   "title": "Ml Model Diagnostics Handbook",
   "text": "3. Regularization Strength in scikit-learn\nIn scikit-learn LogisticRegression the parameter C is the inverse of the regularization strength: a\nsmaller C means stronger regularization, and the default is C=1.0. For Ridge regression the\nparameter alpha works the opposite way: a larger alpha means stronger shrinkage.\nL2 regularization (ridge) shrinks all weights toward zero; L1 regularization (lasso) can set some\nweights exactly to zero and therefore performs feature selection.",
